<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={assigns[:current_user]}>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>{gettext("Support")}</h1>

    <p>
      <.rich text={
        gettext(
          "Traveling Poet is run by one person. Write to %{address} and you will get an answer from him, usually within a day or two. It helps to say which poet is yours and what you saw.",
          address: marker(:address)
        )
      }>
        <:part name="address">
          <a class="link" href={"mailto:#{@contact}"}>{@contact}</a>
        </:part>
      </.rich>
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("My poet has not written anything yet")}</h2>
    <p>
      {gettext(
        "A new poet needs a few minutes to set out and write its first page. The journal shows where it is while you wait. After that a new page arrives once a day, in the morning of the place your poet is in."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("My poet stopped writing")}</h2>
    <p>
      {gettext(
        "Each day's journey costs credits, and a poet that runs out rests until there are more. Your balance and recent activity are under Credits in Settings. If the balance is fine and a day was still missed, write in: it is usually something on our side, and missed days are not charged."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Something in an entry is wrong")}</h2>
    <p>
      {gettext(
        "The poet's pages are written by a language model from sources it read, and it can be mistaken. Mark the passage in the journal and the poet revises it, or tell it in the chat. If an entry contains something that should not be there at all, write to the address above."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("Notifications")}</h2>
    <p>
      {gettext(
        "Turn them on or off under Notifications in Settings. You can also pair Telegram there and have each day's page sent to you as a message."
      )}
    </p>

    <h2>{gettext("My data and my account")}</h2>
    <p>
      <.rich text={
        gettext(
          "What is kept and why is in the %{privacy}; the rules of the service are in the %{terms}. To delete your account and everything in it, open Settings, go to Account and choose Delete account. It takes effect at once and cannot be undone.",
          privacy: marker(:privacy),
          terms: marker(:terms)
        )
      }>
        <:part name="privacy">
          <.link navigate={~p"/privacy"} class="link">{gettext("privacy policy")}</.link>
        </:part>
        <:part name="terms">
          <.link navigate={~p"/terms"} class="link">{gettext("terms")}</.link>
        </:part>
      </.rich>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
